  "glossaryTerms": [
    {
      "slug": "cluster",
      "term": "Cluster",
      "definition": "Three trebles worked into the same chain-space, joined at the top. The basic building block of the granny square."
    },
    {
      "slug": "chain-space",
      "term": "Chain space",
      "definition": "The gap created by skipping a chain or chains. Corner chain-2 spaces hold the corner cluster pairs; side chain-1 spaces separate cluster pairs along the sides."
    }
  ],
  "techniqueSlugs": ["crochet-magic-ring", "crochet-working-in-the-round"],
  "criticalTechniques": ["crochet-magic-ring"],
  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The six-round granny square lands at 15 cm in DK cotton on a 4 mm hook after steam-blocking, which makes it the standard cushion-front motif: three squares across three rows fills a 40 x 40 cm cushion panel without gaps. Each round adds one more "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [{ "type": "glossaryTooltip", "attrs": { "termSlug": "cluster" } }],
            "text": "cluster"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " group per side, so round 6 has five side clusters on each of the four edges and 24 cluster groups in total."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The construction follows the same rules as every granny square: corner "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [{ "type": "glossaryTooltip", "attrs": { "termSlug": "chain-space" } }],
            "text": "chain-space"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " pairs hold a (3tr, ch 2, 3tr) corner group every round; side chain-1 spaces hold a 3tr side cluster group. The only thing that changes round by round is how many side cluster groups sit between each pair of corners."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "infoPanel",
        "attrs": {
          "tone": "tip",
          "title": "Materials for one motif",
          "body": "About 12 g of DK-weight cotton in one to six colours. A 4 mm crochet hook (UK 8, US G/6). Tapestry needle. Scissors. A blocking mat and pins are worth using at this size."
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Gauge" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Each finished six-round granny square measures 15 × 15 cm in DK-weight cotton with a 4 mm hook, after a light steam-block. Swatch at least one motif before starting a cushion project — a few millimetres off per square adds up across nine squares."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Stitches used" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          { "type": "listItem", "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "chain (ch) — UK and US shared." }] }] },
          { "type": "listItem", "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "slip stitch (sl st) — UK and US shared." }] }] },
          { "type": "listItem", "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "treble (tr) — UK; called double crochet (dc) in US patterns." }] }] },
          { "type": "listItem", "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "magic ring (MR) — adjustable starting loop; no centre hole." }] }] }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Pattern" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Worked in the round, right side facing throughout. Ch 3 at the start of each round counts as the first treble of the first cluster. Do not turn."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 3 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Round 1" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Form a magic ring. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). Work 2 tr into the ring. *Ch 2, 3 tr into the ring*; repeat from * to * twice more. Ch 2, sl st to top of beg ch-3 to join. Pull tail to close ring. (12 tr, 4 ch-2 corner spaces.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 3 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Round 2" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st across next 2 tr and into first ch-2 corner sp. Ch 3. Into same sp work 2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr. *Ch 1, into next ch-2 corner sp work (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr)*; repeat from * to * twice more. Ch 1, sl st to top of beg ch-3 to join. (24 tr, 4 ch-2 corner spaces, 4 ch-1 side spaces.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 3 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Round 3" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into first ch-2 corner sp. Ch 3. Into same sp work 2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr. Ch 1. *Into next ch-1 side sp work 3 tr. Ch 1. Into next ch-2 corner sp work (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr). Ch 1.* Repeat from * to * twice more. Into next ch-1 side sp work 3 tr. Ch 1. Sl st to top of beg ch-3. (36 tr, 4 ch-2 corner spaces, 8 ch-1 side spaces.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 3 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Round 4" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into first ch-2 corner sp. Ch 3. Into same sp work 2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr. Ch 1. *[Into next ch-1 side sp work 3 tr. Ch 1.] twice. Into next ch-2 corner sp work (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr). Ch 1.* Repeat from * to * twice more. [Into next ch-1 side sp work 3 tr. Ch 1.] twice. Sl st to top of beg ch-3. (48 tr, 4 ch-2 corner spaces, 12 ch-1 side spaces.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 3 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Round 5" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into first ch-2 corner sp. Ch 3. Into same sp work 2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr. Ch 1. *[Into next ch-1 side sp work 3 tr. Ch 1.] three times. Into next ch-2 corner sp work (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr). Ch 1.* Repeat from * to * twice more. [Into next ch-1 side sp work 3 tr. Ch 1.] three times. Sl st to top of beg ch-3. (60 tr, 4 ch-2 corner spaces, 16 ch-1 side spaces.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 3 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Round 6" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into first ch-2 corner sp. Ch 3. Into same sp work 2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr. Ch 1. *[Into next ch-1 side sp work 3 tr. Ch 1.] four times. Into next ch-2 corner sp work (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr). Ch 1.* Repeat from * to * twice more. [Into next ch-1 side sp work 3 tr. Ch 1.] four times. Sl st to top of beg ch-3. (72 tr, 4 ch-2 corner spaces, 20 ch-1 side spaces.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Chart" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The chart reads outward from the magic ring. Corner chain-2 spaces mark the four corners on every round; chain-1 spaces between clusters along the sides increase by one per edge per round."
          }
        ]
      },
